[h1]Armory - data shell (companion to the Armory editor)[/h1]

[b]Read this first:[/b] this Workshop item is only a small, data-only mod shell. It adds no soldiers, weapons or textures by itself and changes nothing in your game when subscribed. The editor that does the actual work is a separate, free, open-source desktop tool called [b]Armory[/b] (download links are on the page where you found this item).

[h2]What Armory does[/h2]
Armory is a local app (Python + your web browser) for [b]Dynamic Conquest[/b] campaign saves. It lets you change, per soldier, squad or role:
[list]
[*] Weapons, sidearm, launcher, backup gun, headgear, grenades, medical items, tools (ammo follows the weapon)
[*] Uniform (skin) and rank (veterancy)
[*] Skills: weapon skill, toughness, anti-tank rank, specialties
[*] Name, unit-card icon, ability tag, portrait
[/list]
The result is written as a [b]new copy[/b] of your save. Your original is never overwritten unless you explicitly choose to, and then a backup is made first.

[h2]What this Workshop item is for[/h2]
Armory generates a small data-only mod called [b]armory_breeds[/b] so that supply crates keep refilling soldiers whose gear you changed. This shell only exists so the mod folder has the expected structure on your PC. Armory writes its own generated data into the game's mods folder when you save; nothing generated is stored here.

[h2]Safety[/h2]
[list]
[*] Data only: no DLLs, no executables, no scripts run by the game.
[*] Armory itself never injects into or patches the game.
[*] Saves are copied, not overwritten. Restart the game after saving if it was open, because mods are read at startup.
[*] Switch on the [b]Armory soldier breeds[/b] mod in the game's mod list before loading your Armory copy. The editor creates it when you save.
[*] Intended for single-player Conquest.
[/list]

[h2]Status / honesty section[/h2]
Confirmed in game (German saves): loadout edits, uniform, rank, skills, names, crate refill for edited soldiers.
[b]Not yet verified in game:[/b] portraits, unit-card icon changes, ability-tag effects, the on-screen labels of generated soldier types, and non-German nations (Soviet, British, American, Finnish).
Please keep your own save backups.

[h2]Links[/h2]
Armory is open source (MIT). Download the editor, read the code and report bugs here: [url=https://github.com/Sajuuk2033/armory-goh]https://github.com/Sajuuk2033/armory-goh[/url]

